WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:06.390
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Agents of SHIELD finally revealed what the

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:13.330
Clairvoyant was, we got a good look at an
upgraded Deathlok and there was another Winter

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.330
Soldier tie in.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.179
It was pretty easy to miss but I’ll explain
during my top moments.

00:00:19.179 --> 00:00:23.730
Also in lieu of a bonus Marvel Movie video
I’m doing a Winter Soldier review later

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.730
this week.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:29.829
Be sure to subscribe to get it if you're just
finding me for the first time.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:33.800
Normally I try to do bonus Marvel videos on
Tuesdays but when really huge stuff like The

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.630
Walking Dead Finale happens I have to push
stuff around to make room.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:38.620
So let’s start with Top 5 Moments and then
I’ll do my review.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.760
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.760
Here we go.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.130
Number 5 - Winter Soldier Crossover scene.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:49.140
If you blinked you may have missed it, that
scene with Agent Stillwell where he said,

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.910
looks like I have a boat to catch.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.710
It refers to the scene at the beginning of
Winter Soldier where Chris Evans has to rescue

00:00:54.710 --> 00:01:00.160
a bunch of hostages and capture Batroc The
Leaper another notable comic book character.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.439
I love that they do these movie integrations,
sometimes they’re hard to spot.

00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:09.130
I think they’re more interesting when the
crossover moment is something critical to

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:14.659
the plot of both the story going on in the
show and whatever the plot of the movie is.

00:01:14.659 --> 00:01:21.860
I didn’t really feel like Agent Stillwell
needed to be there other than to be Bill Paxton’s

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:26.729
punching bag and to drop that quick line about
the boat in Winter Soldier.

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:29.979
High Fives for the effort though.

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:33.400
Number 4 - Skye becomes a full SHIELD Agent.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.630
One of the few positive moments in the episode.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:38.400
I love the bond that Coulson has formed with
her.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.410
He really is like her surrogate Dad now.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:48.531
If it was unclear, yes they only made her
an Agent so she could access the Index, but

00:01:48.531 --> 00:01:50.860
she’s good going forward, they’re not
going to take that away.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:57.130
I also loved the follow up talk she had with
Garrett about things coming Full Circle.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.530
It’s like Bill Paxton had foreshadowing
tattooed on his forehead.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.510
He’s so much fun to watch though.

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:08.819
All of his compliments to her about inspiring
Ward while Ward was trying to inspire her

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:09.819
were genuine.

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:16.319
Despite the comic book version of his character
being really shady, he is happy to see her

00:02:16.319 --> 00:02:17.490
become an Agent.

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:20.230
Number 3 - Deathlok Armors Up

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:25.220
The best thing about the Mike Peterson Deathlok
scenes are the interaction he has with the

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:30.319
tech, like watching him react to the parts
bond with his skeleton and nervous system.

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:35.880
I don’t care about all the explosions or
watching him run up and down stairs or jump

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.990
super high.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:42.040
The armature was a really nice comic book
addition to his arsenal, but it was Skye’s

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.490
look at him beneath the skin that really stood
out.

00:02:45.490 --> 00:02:47.700
He really is full on cyborg at this point.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.750
They grafted all those parts on to his skeleton.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:55.980
I fully expect them to redeem him at some
point, and he’ll just be a tortured hero

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.620
for the rest of the series, however long it
goes on.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.400
Like if you ever watch Angel with David Boreanaz.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.650
Only on Agents of SHIELD it’s Gunn who end
up being tortured by the memory of all the

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.740
people he’s killed.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:13.830
What I’m saying is that J August Richards
is kind of playing the Angel role on SHIELD

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:14.830
now.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:15.830
Which is really cool.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:17.360
I wonder if Joss Whedon is going to edit any
his lines.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.910
Everyone be sure to listen for Angel references.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:24.410
Number 2 - May Is Outed As The Double Agent

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:30.849
We knew what she was up to after TAHITI, but
it took this long for Coulson to find out.

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:33.520
I liked that the explanation was much more
complicated.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:40.459
She’s not just spying for HYDRA or something,
there’s this big running plot going on about

00:03:40.459 --> 00:03:42.770
SHIELD being eaten alive from the inside.

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:49.489
The cancer of SHIELD is the clairvoyant and
the organization they work for.

00:03:49.489 --> 00:03:53.620
Some of that is revealed in the Winter Soldier,
so make sure to go see it if you haven’t

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.620
already.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.159
They actually reveal the identity of the person
behind the clairvoyant during it, which I

00:03:59.159 --> 00:04:01.700
think kind of cheats the people who have been
watching the show.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.120
You can let me know if you agree.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:12.489
But 
the rest of the season will be all about this

00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:14.440
internal uprising in SHIELD.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.150
The next episode is even called Turn, Turn,
Turn.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.459
As in Agents turning on each other.

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:21.780
Just like Garrett was talking about with Skye.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.770
May is just part of that.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:28.350
Based on the Victoria Hand reveal at the end,
I think May was talking to her all along.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.050
I don’t think either one of them is a double
Agent for Hydra, I just think Hand doesn’t

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:33.500
trust anyone and is using may to monitor Coulson.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.680
She just doesn’t trust Couslon and Coulson
doesn trust her.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:37.970
Turn Turn Turn.

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:43.770
and my Number 1 moment, The Clairvoyant is
a SHIELD Agent.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:48.650
So this was also a confusing moment, but that
man in the chair was Brad Dourif.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.440
The actor playing Thomas Nash.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:52.910
He’s not a comic book character.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:57.650
When he said Poe was the one that started
calling him the Clairvoyant he was being truthful.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.889
The twist is that he’s not the real clairvoyant.

00:05:00.889 --> 00:05:03.720
It’s someone or something inside SHIELD.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.389
If you didn’t see it I did a silly video
suggesting Loki was the clairvoyant.

00:05:08.389 --> 00:05:09.800
It was just for fun.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:16.750
My real assertion was that it was a form of
AI, just because Marvel is trying to tee up

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:22.259
the idea of AI to get everyone ready mentally
for Age of Ultron next year.

00:05:22.259 --> 00:05:26.590
I don’t want to spoil Winter Soldier, but
if you’ve seen it you know who I’m talking

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.590
about.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:30.880
Couslon says it himself, it’s someone who
has access to all of SHIELD’s databases

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:31.880
and information.

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:36.669
That’s why Nick Fury gave Couslon the bus
and told him to make a team to go off the

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:37.669
grid.

00:05:37.669 --> 00:05:40.270
It was a way to circumvent what the clairvoyant
was doing.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.820
Now it’s your turn though.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.639
What was your favorite moment?

00:05:43.639 --> 00:05:47.650
Deathlok, Sneaky May or the big Clairvoyant
reveal.

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:50.729
Just to be clear it’s not Victoria Hand.

00:05:50.729 --> 00:05:54.010
She was just remote piloting the bus.

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:58.300
Overall I give the episode a B plus for picking
up the pace.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:02.460
I think this SHIELD civil war that will play
out over the rest of the season will address

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.150
all of the complaints people have had about
the show.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:07.639
I love how Skye’s character has developed.

00:06:07.639 --> 00:06:12.520
Supposedly Chloe Bennett even revealed that
the blue alien was Kree, meaning she has Kree

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:16.860
blood flowing through her veins.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:18.509
She retracted her statement later.

00:06:18.509 --> 00:06:23.070
But most news sites say the way she said it
was legit.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:26.430
So let’s just say Kree and stick with that.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:32.680
I always love Ming Na, but May just got even
more interesting post-cougar town sexy time

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:33.680
with Ward.

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:36.550
And I love seeing pissed of Coulson.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:39.510
If you remember that first Marvel One Shot
he did for Thor.

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:40.510
In the convenience store.

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:44.790
I want to see a Coulson fight scene like that.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:48.389
It was called Funny Thing Happened on the
Way To Thor’s Hammer.

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:51.840
But let me know what your final thoughts are
on the episode and SHIELD in general right

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.840
now.

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:56.319
Do you think it’s gotten a lot better with
all the intrigue and action they’ve added?

00:06:56.319 --> 00:06:58.910
Like I said, Winter Soldier review coming
this week.

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:02.400
Probably late Thursday Night.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:13.449
In the meantime click here for the last episode
of SHIELD and click here for the Winter Soldier

00:07:13.449 --> 00:07:14.449
trailer.

00:07:14.449 --> 00:07:16.690
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:16.720
High Fives!

